    {
      "text": "I. INTRODUCTION",
      "bbox": [
        135.61495971679688,
        379.325439453125,
        213.3667449951172,
        388.23199462890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Autonomous and highly automated systems inherently de-",
      "bbox": [
        58.921958923339844,
        394.18243408203125,
        300.0168151855469,
        403.0889892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pend on effectively incorporating rigorous guarantees on the",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        406.1374206542969,
        300.01641845703125,
        415.0439758300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance and safety through formal veriﬁcation and vali-",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        418.0924072265625,
        300.01641845703125,
        426.99896240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dation methods. For instance, in order to ensure collision-free",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        430.0473937988281,
        300.0164489746094,
        438.9539489746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "paths, advanced driver-assistance systems need to be capable",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        442.00238037109375,
        300.01654052734375,
        450.908935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of anticipating all potential actions of the driver without overly",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        453.9573669433594,
        300.01641845703125,
        462.8639221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conservative assumptions. This requires performing on-line",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        465.9133605957031,
        300.01641845703125,
        474.8199157714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reachability analysis, i.e., computation of states that these",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        477.86834716796875,
        300.0164794921875,
        486.77490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "vehicles can reach within a given time interval. It can also",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        489.8233337402344,
        300.0164489746094,
        498.7298889160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "serve as a supervisory mechanism for any motion planner",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        501.7783203125,
        300.0163879394531,
        510.68487548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that incorporates deep learning. Going beyond the realm of",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        513.7332763671875,
        300.0163879394531,
        522.6398315429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "autonomous driving, reachability analysis has shown promise",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        525.6882934570312,
        300.0165100097656,
        534.5948486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as a tool for formal veriﬁcation of a wide variety of systems.",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        537.644287109375,
        300.01654052734375,
        546.5508422851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Applications of reachability analysis include safety, correct-",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        549.5993041992188,
        300.0164794921875,
        558.505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ness, and controller synthesis problems involving intricate",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        561.5543212890625,
        300.0164489746094,
        570.4608764648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "speciﬁcations or robotic systems such as autonomous aircraft",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        573.50927734375,
        300.0164794921875,
        582.4158325195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and cars, medical robots, and personal-assistance robots.",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        585.4642944335938,
        280.42999267578125,
        594.370849609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Typically the state of a system is not fully observable, e.g., a",
      "bbox": [
        58.921958923339844,
        597.1832885742188,
        300.0169372558594,
        606.08984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "car might not have precise knowledge about its position. Thus,",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        609.1383056640625,
        300.0164489746094,
        618.0448608398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conducting accurate reachability analysis by deﬁnition requires",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        621.09326171875,
        300.0164489746094,
        629.9998168945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reasoning about all possible trajectories from every possible",
      "bbox": [
        48.95895767211914,
        633.0482788085938,
        300.0183410644531,
        641.954833984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state. Reasoning about all possible behaviors of a system",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        645.0042724609375,
        300.0164794921875,
        653.9108276367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "renders reachability analysis computationally intractable in",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        656.9592895507812,
        300.0164794921875,
        665.8658447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "practice [3]. This computational challenge is further com-",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        668.914306640625,
        300.0164794921875,
        677.8208618164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pounded by the generally large size and high complexity",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        680.8692626953125,
        300.0164794921875,
        689.7758178710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the system in consideration, and the practical need to",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        692.8242797851562,
        300.0164489746094,
        701.7308349609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obtain veriﬁcation results in a reasonably short time (i.e.,",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        704.779296875,
        300.01654052734375,
        713.6858520507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "seconds or minutes, not days) for the sake of, for example,",
      "bbox": [
        48.95896911621094,
        716.7352905273438,
        300.0165100097656,
        725.641845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(a) (1 −ε) = 0.2",
      "bbox": [
        342.0090026855469,
        285.0782165527344,
        404.957275390625,
        293.73974609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(b) (1 −ε) = 0.4",
      "bbox": [
        469.7959899902344,
        285.0782165527344,
        533.2472534179688,
        293.73974609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(c) (1 −ε) = 0.6",
      "bbox": [
        342.0090026855469,
        371.0182189941406,
        404.957275390625,
        379.67974853515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(d) (1 −ε) = 0.8",
      "bbox": [
        468.2650146484375,
        371.0182189941406,
        531.7163696289062,
        379.67974853515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 1: (a)-(d): A 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, and 0.8-approximation respec-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9730529785156,
        388.1639709472656,
        563.032470703125,
        397.22991943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tively, of the reachable set of a unicycle car. The set of initial",
      "bbox": [
        311.9729919433594,
        400.2783508300781,
        563.0303955078125,
        409.1849060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditions is taken to be the unit cube around the origin.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9729919433594,
        412.23333740234375,
        546.25341796875,
        421.139892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "real-time motion planning. These computational challenges in",
      "bbox": [
        311.9729919433594,
        454.2303466796875,
        563.030517578125,
        463.13690185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conjunction with the need to obtain provably valid results",
      "bbox": [
        311.9729919433594,
        466.18634033203125,
        563.0303344726562,
        475.0928955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "motivate the development of approximation schemes with",
      "bbox": [
        311.9729919433594,
        478.1413269042969,
        563.0315551757812,
        487.0478820800781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "provable guarantees for reachability analysis.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        490.0963134765625,
        498.1536865234375,
        499.00286865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this paper, we consider the problem of efﬁciently com-",
      "bbox": [
        321.93597412109375,
        504.3503112792969,
        563.0308837890625,
        513.2568969726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "puting the approximate forward reachable set of a continuous",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        516.3062744140625,
        563.0303344726562,
        525.2128295898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "system, i.e., the set of states that can be reached by a safe",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        528.2612915039062,
        563.0305786132812,
        537.1678466796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "trajectory from any of the speciﬁed initial states. Motivated by",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        540.21630859375,
        563.0303955078125,
        549.1228637695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scenarios where under-approximations of the reachable set are",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        552.1712646484375,
        563.0294799804688,
        561.0778198242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "desired, e.g., in the case of checking feasibility of prospective",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        564.1262817382812,
        563.0304565429688,
        573.0328369140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "motion plans, our problem formulation considers generating",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        576.081298828125,
        563.0304565429688,
        584.9878540039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "provably accurate under-approximations, see Fig. 1 for an",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        588.0372924804688,
        563.030517578125,
        596.94384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "example. In particular, our work imposes minimal assumptions",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        599.9923095703125,
        563.0304565429688,
        608.8988647460938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and is capable of handling any type of nonlinear dynamics as",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        611.947265625,
        563.0303955078125,
        620.8538208007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "well as arbitrarily non-convex regions of states. In this regard,",
      "bbox": [
        311.97296142578125,
        623.9022827148438,
        563.0303344726562,
        632.808837890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
